public class TextUtil {
    public static boolean lastCharIsWhitespace(String text) {
        if (text == null || text.isEmpty()) {
            return true;
        }
        return Character.isWhitespace(text.charAt(text.length() - 1));
    }

    public static String trimText(String text) {
        int start = 0;
        while (start < text.length() && Character.isWhitespace(text.charAt(start))) {
            start++;
        }
        if (start >= text.length()) {
            return "";
        }
        int end = text.length() - 1;
        while (end >= 0 && Character.isWhitespace(text.charAt(end))) {
            end--;
        }
        return text.substring(start, end + 1);
    }

    public static class TextNode {
        private String text;

        public String getText() {
            return text;
        }

        public void setText(String text) {
            this.text = text;
        }

        public static TextNode lastCharIsWhitespace(TextNode node) {
            if (node == null || node.getText() == null) {
                return null;
            }
            return new TextNode() {
                @Override
                public String getText() {
                    return super.getText();
                }

                @Override
                public void setText(String text) {
                    this.text = Character.isWhitespace(text.charAt(text.length() - 1)) ? text : "";
                    super.setText(this.text);
                }
            };
        }
    }
}
```

This code includes three methods:

- `lastCharIsWhitespace`: Checks if the last character in a given string is a whitespace.
- `trimText`: Trims leading and trailing whitespaces from a string.
- `TextNode.lastCharIsWhitespace`: A static method that modifies the `text` field of a `TextNode` object to remove the last character if it's a whitespace.

You can use these methods as follows:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "   Hello World!  ";
        System.out.println(TextUtil.lastCharIsWhitespace(text)); // true
        System.out.println(TextUtil.trimText(text)); // "Hello World!"
    }
}
```

In the `main` method, we create a string with leading and trailing whitespaces. We then print the result of `lastCharIsWhitespace` to check if the last character is a whitespace, and print the result of `trimText` to remove the leading and trailing whitespaces.
